# Go build/module cache inside repo
.go/
.cache/

# Build output. `go build ./...` writes each main package's binary into the
# working directory, so cmd/<name> becomes ./<name> at the repo root.
#
# Anchored. Unanchored it also matched web/dist, and git does not descend into
# an excluded directory — so the un-ignore below could not have rescued the
# sentinel, and a checkout with no Node would have failed to compile with
# "pattern all:dist: no matching files found".
/dist/
/swarmcli-cd

# Nothing named /controller belongs here: the entry point is the `controller`
# package at the repository root, and ignoring that path would silently drop it.

# The UI's build output, except the sentinel: `//go:embed all:dist` needs the
# directory to be non-empty on a tree that has never run Vite, and `all:` is
# what makes a dotfile count towards that. Plus the dependency tree, which
# `npm ci` reinstalls from the committed lockfile.
web/dist/*
!web/dist/.gitkeep
web/ui/node_modules/

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

site/

# Devcontainer metadata
.devcontainer/*.log
.devcontainer/devcontainer.local.json
.devcontainer/certs/*.pem
.devcontainer/certs/*.crt
.devcontainer/certs/corporate-proxy.crt
.devcontainer/shared/*

debug.log
